  // The clamshell in two frames meeting at its hinge axis: the lower half's (x right, y from the hinge toward its front
  // edge running negative, z out of the control face), turned -60 degrees about x so the half lies 30 degrees up from
  // level on the stand; and the upper half's (y from the hinge up the screen, z out of the glass), turned -30 degrees,
  // the 150-degree stop. The halves are 82 and 80 mm long, 13.3 and 10.4 mm thick, chamfered 1.2 mm round every rim;
  // each half begins 1.6 mm from the axis. The dark glass covers the upper half's face to 2 mm of its edges, and the
  // screen's picture (screen 1) lies on it 43.6 mm from the axis to its centre (1 mm above the glass's centre), 0.3 mm
  // proud. The lower half carries the d-pad at (-26.5, -41.6) mm in its frame, A and B at (30, -37.1) and
  // (18.5, -45.1), select and start at (-33.5, -67.6) and (-21.5, -67.6), five speaker slots at (26, -69.6), the power
  // light by the hinge, the shoulder keys at its back corners and the cartridge out of its front edge.
  prototype "device-advanced-gaming-brick" {
    document {
      name: "ADVANCED GAMING BRICK"
      schema: "puck.creation.v1"
      palette: advancedPalette
      shape Prism "lower-shell" {
